{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Description rewritten and re-based on `origin/main` `403719c01ce`. Four defects, one of which would have broken a live contract.\n\n**1. The story would have deleted `load_config`'s tombstone scan.** The old Approach said \"KEEP `_env_signature` (minus `:382-385`, deleted by the alias story)\". On the current tree `:382-385` is not in `_env_signature` (`:279-303`) at all — it is inside `load_config` (`:371-405`), and it is the retired-input scan:\n\n```\n382|     from rebar._deprecations import raise_or_warn_env, raise_or_warn_file, tombstones\n384|     raise_or_warn_env(os.environ)\n385|     # Registry behavior, not a hardcoded filename, decides file warning/refusal.\n```\n\n`_env_signature` carries a comment at `:296-302` saying its tombstone loop exists so \"the top-of-`load_config` tombstone scan re-fires\". The two halves are a pair. Deleting one breaks the retired-env-var contract while the other silently keeps paying to invalidate the cache for a scan that is gone. `cb2b` was corrected to KEEP it as well; both stories now say so, and a tombstone regression test is in Testing.\n\n**2. The module-size premise is dead.** Context asserted `config.py` \"is exactly 800 lines … so this story must net-shrink it\". It is **624**. AC4's `wc -l … <= 778` therefore passed with zero work — the third vacuous AC found in this epic. Replaced with a strict delta against the measured pre-state of 624. The complexity clause is kept but re-justified: `config.py` has **no** entries in `.github/complexity-baseline.json`, so `new=0` is not evidence about existing code — it binds only the newly added `_compose`/`_winning_label`/`_validation_tokens`.\n\n**3. There is a FOURTH copy of the discovery walk, and AC1 could not see it.** The plan named three. `_config_resolvers.py::_snapshot_table` (`:100-131`) runs the same `user_config_path()` / `is_file()` / `_discover_project_config` / `_read_toml_table` sequence at `:114-126` for the `[snapshot]` section. AC1's grep was scoped `-- src/rebar/config.py src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py`, so the fourth copy would have survived untouched and AC1 would still have passed — while the story's own title promises \"one file-discovery generator\". Scope and AC1 now cover it. Its deliberate in-body import (`:110`, documented at `:105-109` as preserving `monkeypatch.setattr` late binding and avoiding an import cycle) must be preserved; the rewrite says so explicitly.\n\n**4. AC1 was unrunnable as written.** It required the grep to \"show only `_config_probe_paths`/`_validation_tokens`\" — but a `git grep` of call sites cannot print a function name, and `_validation_tokens` does not exist yet. Run verbatim it returns 4 hits (`show_config.py:93`, `config.py:42,268,587`), none of them those names. Worse, the second alternation branch `user_config_path().is_file` matches **zero** lines anywhere in `src`: the real idiom is split over two lines (`up = user_config_path()` then `if up.is_file():`), so half the pattern was dead. AC1 is now a hit-count delta, 6 to 3, with every pre-state hit enumerated.\n\n**Citation drift (`083620b0` -> `403719c01ce`):**\n\n| plan said | actual |\n|---|---|\n| `_resolve` `:442-466` | `:347-368` |\n| `resolve_with_sources` `:774-800` | `:603-624` |\n| `_ordered_layers` `:330-359` | `:249-276` |\n| discovery copy `config.py:343-355` | `:260-272` |\n| `read_reserved_section` `:749-761` | `:575-594` |\n| `load_config` `:469-519` | `:371-405` |\n| provenance loop `:791-799` | `:615-623` |\n| validation tokens `:451-466` | `:353-367` |\n| `_discover_project_config` `_config_sources.py:217` | `:166-197` |\n| `compose_operation_snapshot` `:203-227` | `:165-193` |\n| bindings `:230-311` | `:194-274` — the old cite ran **37 lines past EOF** (file is 274) |\n| `test_config_show.py:157-164` | `:141-153` (`:157` is the text-output test) |\n| `test_llm_config_pointer.py:221-250` | `:221-240` (`:241` is a different test) |\n| `docs/reuse-surface.md:587-592` | `:614` — `:587` is the OperationSnapshot \"Construction\" heading; the `_config_sources` ownership section is `:612-614` |\n\n**Verified correct, left alone.** `show_config.py::_raw_toml_layers` really is still at `:86-102` — the one cite that did not move. ADR 0098 §1 `:83-96` is in range and says what the plan claims (§1 spans `:81-113`); only the filename needed completing to `0098-operation-scoped-config-and-provider-composition.md`. `test_config_perf.py:185-227` correctly covers both warm-resolution tests, and `_ordered_layers` is genuinely monkeypatched at `:195,201,217,223`, so keeping its name and signature is a real constraint. The decision to leave `_operation_config.py` alone is right.\n\nThat is all four remaining stories in this epic carrying at least one acceptance criterion that could not certify its own work."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793424995881008842,"uuid":"265d8771-3d8d-4114-9364-fe535530cf68"}